      "writtenOn": "2019-11-07T21:47:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The distinction between Global and Local is definitely fuzzy.  In this case, it is a local characteristic of the module that is causing the build system to add the flag.  This particular case probably makes more sense for Global though, since it is not a characteristic that is controlled by an Android.bp property.  But in cases like \"rtti: true\", which would cause the build system to add -frtti, that should be treated as a local property.  Same with \"local_include_dirs\".",
